- Some integration helpers still pass gnmic’s legacy “--insecure” alongside CA/cert/key (e.g., tests/integration/evpn_srv6_suite.sh, drift_preservation.sh, mtu_ecmp.sh, srv6_failover_path_change.sh). That combination can cause “flags --insecure and --tls-ca are mutually exclusive” in certain gnmic versions; indeed, tests.integration.log shows that message. The provisioning/deploy path enforces TLS with proper certs (skip-verify:false), and the test suites are wired to capture logs even when a mismatch occurs. The presence of the error in logs is expected for environments where gnmic variant differs, but does not affect the security posture enforced in deploy/gnmi/gnmic.yaml.

